message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Silice-Neuro3D-Cube: CPU research models for laser-written optical silica networks"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
authors:
  - family-names: "Angulo de Lafuente"
    given-names: "Francisco"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Agnuxo1/Silice-Neuro3D-Cube"
url: "https://github.com/Agnuxo1/Silice-Neuro3D-Cube"
keywords:
  - femtosecond laser writing
  - optical waveguides
  - fused silica
  - beam propagation method
  - coupled-mode theory
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  Numerical research on a passive optical network written with femtosecond
  laser inside fused silica. The repository contains CPU models, bounded
  CUDA tests, retained negative results and their audits. No fabricated
  device, measured optical system or validated neural network is claimed.
  Version 0.2.0 adds the scientific closure of 2026-10-13: preregistered
  kill tests (depth and crossings of 3D versus planar meshes, energy per
  multiply-accumulate, in-situ calibration, state of the art), a claims
  ledger, the closure kit (agentkit/) and an English manuscript. The energy
  advantage hypothesis was discarded by its registered test.
